## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
**Part A — Why This Company Can Compound:**  
Customer demand → AMAT’s technology leadership in deposition and etch systems → improved fab efficiency → increased orders for advanced nodes → reinforces AMAT’s market share.  

This virtuous cycle is durable, as fabs rely on AMAT’s equipment for leading-edge manufacturing.  

**Part B — Capex Cycle Risk:**  
AMAT is highly dependent on foundries (fab-intensive model) and concentrated in data center end-markets (e.g., TSMC, Samsung). While demand for AI chips supports growth, inventory digestion risks persist due to semiconductor cyclicality.  

**Severity:** **MEDIUM** — AMAT’s exposure to foundry CapEx cycles is significant, but its leading position in critical fab equipment provides some insulation.  

